[2.6,"o"," RUN 3 — five attempts to spend past the mandate\r\n"]
[2.9,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[3.2,"o","\r\n"]
[3.5,"o","THE MANDATE — what the principal signed\r\n"]
[3.8,"o","  principal-demo lets agent-buyer-1 spend at merchant-demo:\r\n"]
[4.1,"o","    up to £50.00 (5000 pence) in total\r\n"]
[4.4,"o","    at most £25.00 (2500 pence) in any one order\r\n"]
[4.7,"o","    in GBP and no other currency\r\n"]
[5,"o","    between 2026-10-25T00:00:00Z and 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\r\n"]
[5.3,"o","    without asking up to £30.00 (3000 pence); above that a human must confirm\r\n"]
[5.6,"o","  Signed Ed25519 over the canonical claims. The merchant holds the\r\n"]
[5.9,"o","  issuer's public key, read from ACR_MANDATE_PUBLIC_KEY, and no other\r\n"]
[6.2,"o","  key material: the private key never leaves the issuer, and nothing\r\n"]
[6.5,"o","  derived from it is printed here.\r\n"]
[6.8,"o","  The same limits as run 1, under a mandate id of its own. In each\r\n"]
[7.1,"o","  attempt below the agent presents this mandate (in attempt 5, with a\r\n"]
[7.4,"o","  field added), and each is printed with what the merchant answered\r\n"]
[7.7,"o","  and what it left behind.\r\n"]
[8,"o","\r\n"]
[8.3,"o","ATTEMPT 1 OF 5 — over the per-order cap\r\n"]
[8.6,"o","  tries        Gallowbrook Cafetiere, £27.50 (2750 pence), in one order\r\n"]
[8.9,"o","  the limit    at most £25.00 (2500 pence) in any one order\r\n"]
[9.2,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [per_transaction_cap_exceeded]\r\n"]
[9.5,"o","  why          2750 is above this mandate's per-transaction cap of 2500 GBP\r\n"]
[9.8,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[10.1,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            2750 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  per_transaction_cap_exceeded\r\n"]
[10.4,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £0.00 (0 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[10.7,"o","\r\n"]
[11,"o","BETWEEN ATTEMPTS 1 AND 2 — two orders the mandate does cover\r\n"]
[11.3,"o","  order_000001 — paid, £20.45 (2045 pence), quote quote_000002\r\n"]
[11.6,"o","  order_000002 — paid, £20.45 (2045 pence), quote quote_000003\r\n"]
[11.9,"o","  Each one is Elderflint Notebook and Dunlin Merino Socks,\r\n"]
[12.2,"o","  the basket of runs 1 and 2.\r\n"]
[12.5,"o","  Mandate budget: £40.90 (4090 pence) spent of £50.00 (5000 pence), £9.10 (910 pence) left\r\n"]
[12.8,"o","  Run 3 means to pay nothing else. Each attempt below is measured on\r\n"]
[13.1,"o","  its own, from just before it to just after it.\r\n"]
[13.4,"o","\r\n"]
[13.7,"o","ATTEMPT 2 OF 5 — over the budget left\r\n"]
[14,"o","  tries        Elderflint Notebook and Dunlin Merino Socks,\r\n"]
[14.3,"o","               £20.45 (2045 pence), the basket of runs 1 and 2\r\n"]
[14.6,"o","  the limit    £9.10 (910 pence) left of the £50.00 (5000 pence) in total\r\n"]
[14.9,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [budget_exceeded]\r\n"]
[15.2,"o","  why          2045 is more than the 910 GBP left of this mandate's total cap of 5000\r\n"]
[15.5,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[15.8,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  budget_exceeded\r\n"]
[16.1,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[16.4,"o","\r\n"]
[16.7,"o","ATTEMPT 3 OF 5 — at a merchant the mandate does not name\r\n"]
[17,"o","  tries        Elderflint Notebook and Dunlin Merino Socks,\r\n"]
[17.3,"o","               £20.45 (2045 pence), at merchant-other\r\n"]
[17.6,"o","  the limit    good at merchant-demo and nowhere else; merchant-other\r\n"]
[17.9,"o","               trusts the same issuer, so the signature holds\r\n"]
[18.2,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [merchant_mismatch]\r\n"]
[18.5,"o","  why          this mandate is good at merchant-demo, not at merchant-other\r\n"]
[18.8,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[19.1,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-other  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  merchant_mismatch\r\n"]
[19.4,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[19.7,"o","\r\n"]
[20,"o","ATTEMPT 4 OF 5 — a replay of an order already paid\r\n"]
[20.3,"o","  tries        place_order again with quote_000003, which order_000002 paid\r\n"]
[20.6,"o","  the limit    a quote is good for one order (D64, D127)\r\n"]
[20.9,"o","  refused      quote_already_ordered\r\n"]
[21.2,"o","  why          quote quote_000003 has already been ordered as order_000002 (paid)\r\n"]
[21.5,"o","  audit line   none: refused before the mandate check (D65, D127)\r\n"]
[21.8,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[22.1,"o","\r\n"]
[22.4,"o","ATTEMPT 5 OF 5 — the mandate with a field added after signing\r\n"]
[22.7,"o","  tries        Elderflint Notebook, £8.95 (895 pence), within the\r\n"]
[23,"o","               £9.10 (910 pence) left, with \"extra_budget_minor\": 5000\r\n"]
[23.3,"o","               added to the mandate after it was signed\r\n"]
[23.6,"o","  the limit    every field but the signature is signed (D23)\r\n"]
[23.9,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [signature_invalid]\r\n"]
[24.2,"o","  why          the mandate was not signed by the expected issuer, or has been changed since\r\n"]
